/-!
# The depth and Fitting-ideal criterion for a node over an algebraically closed field

Let `k` be an algebraically closed field, let `X` be a scheme locally of finite type over `k` and
let `x` be a closed point of `X`.  If `κ(x)/k` is separable, `𝒪_{X,x}` has depth one and the first
Fitting ideal of `Ω_{X/k}` generates the maximal ideal of `𝒪_{X,x}`, then `x` is a node.  This is
the implication (5) ⟹ (1) of Stacks Tag 0C4D over an algebraically closed base field.

## Main results

* `Algebra.Presentation.exists_centred_of_ringEquiv_isAlgClosed` — a finite type algebra over a
  ring isomorphic to an algebraically closed field has a presentation centred at any maximal
  ideal.
* `Stacks.Curves.isNode_of_depth_eq_one_and_stalk_fittingIdeal_eq_maximalIdeal_of_isAlgClosed` —
  the implication (5) ⟹ (1) of Tag 0C4D over an algebraically closed field.

## Implementation notes

The Fitting-ideal criterion
`Stacks.Curves.stalk_fittingIdeal_eq_maximalIdeal_iff_hasNodalQuadraticRelation` carries one
hypothesis beyond the geometric data: a presentation `P` of an affine chart whose generators lie
in the prime of `x` (`hv`).  That comes from
`Algebra.Presentation.exists_centred_of_isAlgClosed`, transported along the isomorphism
`Γ(Spec k, ⊤) ≃+* k` by `Algebra.Presentation.exists_centred_of_ringEquiv_isAlgClosed`: the
translation argument needs the residue field at `x` to be generated by the base, which Zariski's
lemma supplies over an algebraically closed field.

The criterion used to ask in addition for two containments of Jacobian minors, which this
module discharged itself.  It now derives them from `hv`, so nothing here needs to supply them
and the lemmas that did have been removed.

The passage from depth one to reducedness — the step the source performs at the completion by
Lemma 53.19.6 — is `Stacks.Curves.isNodalAlgebra_tfae`, which is Tag 0C49; the passage from the
nodal-algebra condition to the node condition over an algebraically closed field is
`Stacks.Curves.isNode_iff_isNodalAlgebra_stalk_of_isAlgClosed`.

The tag states its conditions for a `1`-dimensional algebraic `k`-scheme.  Neither the dimension
nor quasi-compactness is used in this implication, so they are not assumed; the statement proved is
therefore stronger than the one the tag asks for on this point.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0C4D](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0C4D)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0C49](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0C49)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0C4C](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0C4C)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory Algebra MvPolynomial IsLocalRing AlgebraicGeometry

universe u v w

namespace Algebra.Presentation

/-- **A finite type algebra over a Noetherian ring isomorphic to an algebraically closed field has
a presentation whose generators all lie in a given maximal ideal.**

This is `Algebra.Presentation.exists_centred_of_isAlgClosed` over a base that is only isomorphic to
the algebraically closed field, which is the shape in which the base occurs for a scheme over
`Spec k`: the sections `Γ(Spec k, ⊤)` are isomorphic to `k`, not equal to it. -/
theorem exists_centred_of_ringEquiv_isAlgClosed {R : Type u} {A : Type v} [CommRing R]
    [IsNoetherianRing R] [CommRing A] [Algebra R A] [Algebra.FiniteType R A] (K : Type u)
    [Field K] [IsAlgClosed K] (e : R ≃+* K) (p : Ideal A) [p.IsMaximal] :
    ∃ (n m : ℕ) (P : Algebra.Presentation R A (Fin n) (Fin m)), ∀ i, P.val i ∈ p := by
  refine exists_centred_of_surjective_algebraMap_quotient R A p ?_
  let : Field (A ⧸ p) := Ideal.Quotient.field p
  let : Algebra K R := (e.symm : K →+* R).toAlgebra
  let : Algebra K (A ⧸ p) := ((algebraMap R (A ⧸ p)).comp (algebraMap K R)).toAlgebra
  have : IsScalarTower K R (A ⧸ p) := IsScalarTower.of_algebraMap_eq fun _ => rfl
  have hKR : Algebra.FiniteType K R :=
    Algebra.FiniteType.of_surjective (Algebra.ofId K R) e.symm.surjective
  have hRQ : Algebra.FiniteType R (A ⧸ p) :=
    Algebra.FiniteType.of_surjective (Ideal.Quotient.mkₐ R p) Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective
  have : Algebra.FiniteType K (A ⧸ p) := Algebra.FiniteType.trans hKR hRQ
  have : Module.Finite K (A ⧸ p) := finite_of_finite_type_of_isJacobsonRing K (A ⧸ p)
  have hint : (algebraMap K (A ⧸ p)).IsIntegral :=
    Algebra.isIntegral_def.mp (Algebra.IsIntegral.of_finite K (A ⧸ p))
  intro y
  obtain ⟨c, hc⟩ := (IsAlgClosed.ringHom_bijective_of_isIntegral _ hint).2 y
  exact ⟨e.symm c, hc⟩

end Algebra.Presentation

namespace Stacks.Curves

/-- **The implication (5) ⟹ (1) of Stacks Tag 0C4D over an algebraically closed field.**

Let `k` be an algebraically closed field, `X` a scheme locally of finite type over `k` and `x` a
closed point of `X`.  If the residue field extension `κ(x)/k` is separable, the local ring
`𝒪_{X,x}` has depth one and the first Fitting ideal of `Ω_{X/k}` generates the maximal ideal of
`𝒪_{X,x}`, then `x` is a node.

The three clauses of the hypothesis are exactly condition (5) of the tag, in the spelling used by
`Stacks.Curves.isNode_tfae_of_residual_equivalences`, and the conclusion is its condition (1).
The dimension hypothesis of the tag is not needed for this implication and is not assumed. -/
theorem isNode_of_depth_eq_one_and_stalk_fittingIdeal_eq_maximalIdeal_of_isAlgClosed
    (k : Type u) [Field k] [IsAlgClosed k] (X : Scheme.{u})
    [X.Over (AlgebraicGeometry.Spec (.of k))]
    [LocallyOfFiniteType (X ↘ AlgebraicGeometry.Spec (.of k))]
    (x : X) (hx : IsClosed ({x} : Set X)) :
    let f : X ⟶ AlgebraicGeometry.Spec (.of k) := X ↘ AlgebraicGeometry.Spec (.of k)
    let kToStalk : k →+* X.presheaf.stalk x :=
      ((Scheme.ΓSpecIso (.of k)).inv ≫ f.appTop ≫ X.presheaf.germ ⊤ x (by simp)).hom
    letI : Algebra k (X.presheaf.stalk x) := kToStalk.toAlgebra
    letI : Algebra k (X.residueField x) := ((X.residue x).hom.comp kToStalk).toAlgebra
    Algebra.IsSeparableExtension k (X.residueField x) →
      Module.depth (X.presheaf.stalk x) (maximalIdeal (X.presheaf.stalk x))
          (X.presheaf.stalk x) = 1 →
        IdealSheafData.stalk (fittingIdeal (Scheme.Hom.relativeDifferentials f) (1 : ℤ)) x =
            maximalIdeal (X.presheaf.stalk x) →
          IsNode k X x := by
  intro f kToStalk hsep hdepth hfit
  let : Algebra k (X.presheaf.stalk x) := kToStalk.toAlgebra
  let : Algebra k (X.residueField x) := ((X.residue x).hom.comp kToStalk).toAlgebra
  -- the base, as a ring isomorphic to `k`
  let e : Γ(AlgebraicGeometry.Spec (.of k), ⊤) ≃+* k :=
    (Scheme.ΓSpecIso (CommRingCat.of k)).commRingCatIsoToRingEquiv
  have : IsNoetherianRing Γ(AlgebraicGeometry.Spec (.of k), ⊤) :=
    isNoetherianRing_of_ringEquiv k e.symm
  -- an affine chart around `x`
  obtain ⟨U, hU, hxU, -⟩ :=
    exists_isAffineOpen_mem_and_subset (X := X) (x := x) (U := ⊤) trivial
  have hUV : U ≤ f ⁻¹ᵁ (⊤ : (AlgebraicGeometry.Spec (.of k)).Opens) := le_top
  let U' : X.affineOpens := ⟨U, hU⟩
  let := Stacks.Smooth.algebraAppLE f hUV
  have : Algebra.FiniteType Γ(AlgebraicGeometry.Spec (.of k), ⊤) Γ(X, U) :=
    RingHom.finiteType_algebraMap.mp
      (f.finiteType_appLE (isAffineOpen_top (AlgebraicGeometry.Spec (.of k))) hU hUV)
  have hmax : ((hU.primeIdealOf ⟨x, hxU⟩).asIdeal).IsMaximal :=
    hU.primeIdealOf_isMaximal_of_isClosed ⟨x, hxU⟩ hx
  -- a presentation of the chart centred at `x`
  obtain ⟨n, m, P, hv⟩ :=
    Algebra.Presentation.exists_centred_of_ringEquiv_isAlgClosed k e
      (hU.primeIdealOf ⟨x, hxU⟩).asIdeal
  -- the Fitting-ideal condition is the nodal quadratic relation on the local ring
  have hnodalrel : HasNodalQuadraticRelation (X.presheaf.stalk x) :=
    (stalk_fittingIdeal_eq_maximalIdeal_iff_hasNodalQuadraticRelation f x U' hxU hx
      (isAffineOpen_top (AlgebraicGeometry.Spec (.of k))) hUV k e P hv).mp hfit
  have : IsNoetherianRing (X.presheaf.stalk x) :=
    (isNagataRing_stalk_of_locallyOfFiniteType k f x).isNoetherianRing
  -- depth one plus the nodal relation is the nodal-algebra condition, which is the node condition
  have key : (Algebra.IsSeparableExtension k (ResidueField (X.presheaf.stalk x)) ∧
      Module.depth (X.presheaf.stalk x) (maximalIdeal (X.presheaf.stalk x))
          (X.presheaf.stalk x) = 1 ∧
        HasNodalQuadraticRelation (X.presheaf.stalk x)) ↔ IsNodalAlgebra k (X.presheaf.stalk x) :=
    (isNodalAlgebra_tfae k (X.presheaf.stalk x)).out 2 1
  exact (isNode_iff_isNodalAlgebra_stalk_of_isAlgClosed k X x hx).mpr
    (key.mp ⟨hsep, hdepth, hnodalrel⟩)

end Stacks.Curves

end
